            "result_text": "Done! The regex has been saved to `/app/regex.txt`.\n\nHere's how the pattern works:\n\n**IPv4 validation** (`(?:0|[1-9][0-9]?|1[0-9]{2}|2[0-4][0-9]|25[0-5])` repeated 4 times):\n- `0` - single zero\n- `[1-9][0-9]?` - 1-99\n- `1[0-9]{2}` - 100-199\n- `2[0-4][0-9]` - 200-249\n- `25[0-5]` - 250-255\n\n**Date validation** (`\\d{4}-(0[1-9]|1[0-2])-(0[1-9]|[12]\\d|3[01])`):\n- Year: 4 digits\n- Month: 01-12\n- Day: 01-31 (covers Feb's max of 29)\n\n**Key mechanisms**:\n- `(?<![a-zA-Z0-9])` and `(?![a-zA-Z0-9])` - Word boundaries to prevent matching partial dates/IPs\n- `.*?` (lazy) between IPv4 and date to avoid greedy over-matching\n- `(?!.*\\d{4}-...)` - Negative lookahead that only captures the date if no other dates follow it on the same line\n- Single capture group for the date so `re.findall()` returns just the dates\n\nThe pattern uses `re.MULTILINE` flag so `^` and `$` match line boundaries, matching one line at a time."
